    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d560-a2">

                <pb facs="0881" n="753" sameAs="frus:frus1885/pg753"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 394.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Foster to Mr. Elduayen</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">San
                                Ildefonso</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1885-08-20"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 20,
                        1885</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your excellency’s note of the 17th instant, in which you state that
                    as a result of the comparison of <pb facs="0882" n="754" xml:id="pg754"/> data
                    in your ministry, the Spanish plenipotentiary in Washington has been instructed
                    to pay to the Department of State the sum of $7,987.80, as a definitive
                    settlement of the claim for the return of the cattle tax collected by the
                    Spanish consul at Key West.</p>
                <p>Assuring your excellency that I shall have great pleasure in communicating this
                    information to my Government, I remain, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JOHN W. FOSTER.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
